    ===============================================================================
    =             L I M I T A T I O N S   &   S C A L E                           =
    ===============================================================================

     WHAT IS A "NODE"?

       Every asset Lattice discovers = one node on the graph.
       1 catalog + 10 schemas + 500 tables = ~510 nodes
       Typical workspace: 1,000 - 3,000 nodes

       Workspaces organized into catalogs work best with Lattice.
       Scope to specific catalogs in Settings -> Catalog Scope.

     CANVAS RENDERING (ReactFlow):

       < 1,000 nodes     Smooth
       1,000 - 3,000     Good (minor delay on layout changes)
       3,000 - 5,000     Usable (filter by type/catalog)
       5,000+            Use filters, search, or catalog scope

       Hard clip at 2,000 visible nodes (notification shown).

     INGESTION LIMITS:

       +------------------------+---------+--------+---------------------+
       | Setting                | Default | Max    | Configure in        |
       +------------------------+---------+--------+---------------------+
       | Tables / schema        |      50 |  1,000 | Settings -> Scope   |
       | Schemas / catalog      |      20 |    500 | Settings -> Scope   |
       | Jobs                   |     200 |    200 | Not yet configurable|
       | Lineage query limit    |  10,000 |100,000 | Settings -> Advanced|
       | Job backfill limit     |     500 |  5,000 | Settings -> Advanced|
       | Table backfill limit   |   2,000 | 20,000 | Settings -> Advanced|
       +------------------------+---------+--------+---------------------+

       Example: 20K table workspace with defaults =
       ~1,000 primary + 2,000 backfill = ~3,000 of 20K tables.
       Increase in Settings -> Advanced (at your own risk).

     SYSTEM TABLE BLIND SPOTS:

       * Spark-only tables appear "cold"
         (system.query.history = SQL warehouse only)
       * 30-day lineage window
         (monthly jobs may not have edges)
       * Cost attribution is directional
         (BFS graph walk, not per-query accounting)
       * Job reliability is noisy
         (includes retries, cancels, dev/test runs)
       * UC tags + column lineage require grants
         (silently empty if unavailable)


